Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Belfry: the pass's tokens arrive on sign-in; no Lightning
 address or Nostr settings

After signing in, the wallet asks the onboarding service (BELFRY_PASS_URL, GET
/wallet/pass-tokens, NIP-98 signed with the participant's key) for the tokens of their active
passes and redeems them, so a participant who never opened the separate "Get your tokens" link
no longer sees 0 tokens. The settings drop cashu.me's Lightning address (npub.cash), its Nostr
keys, relays and web of trust, Nostr Wallet Connect and Nostr payment requests: village tokens
have no Lightning side and the wallet's Nostr identity is the participant's sign-in.
